# Upstream versions and their source hashes for the self-built container
# engine (PLAN-012 D1/D2).
#
# WHY THESE VERSIONS AND NOT THE DISTRIBUTION'S. This is the point of the whole
# directory: trixie ships podman 5.4.2, crun 1.21, netavark 1.14. Pinning here
# means the engine's version is a decision in this repository rather than a
# consequence of which Debian release the base happens to be. Space is a side
# effect, not the reason.
#
# THIS FILE IS THE UPGRADE INTERFACE. Bump a tag, bump its hash, run the image
# chain, read the verifier. Same shape as os/boards/cx3576/board.env, and for the
# same reason: "which engine is on this device" has to be answerable from the
# tree rather than from a build log.
#
# The hash is of the git TREE at the tag, taken by `git archive` and piped to
# sha256sum inside the build, so it covers the source we actually compile. A
# tag can be moved; a hash cannot.
#
# Hashes recorded 2026-08-23 by the two-step below.
#
# HOW TO BUMP ONE: change the tag, set its hash to the literal string
# `PENDING`, and run `make podman`. The build prints the hash it computed and
# fails; paste it in and run again. That is deliberate — it makes recording a
# hash an act rather than a copy from an upstream page nobody re-checked.
#
# THAT SENTENCE WAS FALSE UNTIL RFCT-108 M2c, and it is worth recording which of
# the two was wrong. os/podman/Dockerfile set `ARG MOS_PODMAN_STRICT=0` and
# refused a PENDING only at 1, so the default behaviour was a WARNING: a bump
# left half-finished produced a green build against whatever the tag pointed at
# that day. The knob's own comment said CI set it — nothing in this repository
# ever did, in any workflow, Makefile target or script. So the code was wrong,
# not the prose: the file said `fails`, `os/build-env/images.env` implements
# exactly that for base images and records why, and a build that warns while its
# documentation says it fails is a build that teaches you to stop reading the
# documentation. The knob is gone and this paragraph now describes the code.

# podman is pinned to the 5.x line, NOT the newest tag. Upstream released
# v6.1.0 on 2026-08-12 and is maintaining both lines — v5.8.6, v6.0.2 and
# v6.1.0 all carry recent dates. 5.8.6 is chosen while this build is being
# brought up so that a failure has one explanation: a build that took a dozen
# iterations to get right should not also be carrying an eleven-day-old major
# version whose behaviour changes nobody here has read.
#
# Moving to 6.x is this file's job and costs two lines — set the tag, set the
# hash to PENDING, run `make podman`, paste the hash it prints. Checked
# 2026-08-23; every other component below IS at its newest upstream release.
PODMAN_VERSION=v5.8.6
PODMAN_SHA256=c2902305ef17a1207ee8c90e645cbbff8ffdf4a2dd493166cdd9cc8b04ef1f8c

CRUN_VERSION=1.29.1
CRUN_SHA256=d5f2f27ea25554ad28c4163749cd3060f39ba48461b5dc6e80cf676b53ba5515

CONMON_VERSION=v2.2.1
CONMON_SHA256=d3e602a1ae17dc73d1ee1b099a7510202878344f4546612547a86daee67be079

# netavark and aardvark-dns move TOGETHER: netavark invokes aardvark-dns and
# writes its configuration, so a version skew between them is a DNS failure
# inside containers rather than a build failure here.
#
# These were pinned to the 1.17 pair while the build targeted musl, because
# aardvark-dns 2.x calls libc::close_range and the libc crate defines that
# symbol for gnu and NOT for musl (measured: 1 occurrence in gnu/mod.rs, 0 in
# musl/mod.rs). Building against glibc removes that constraint entirely, which
# is why the 2.1 pair is back.
NETAVARK_VERSION=v2.1.0
NETAVARK_SHA256=e6abbd7206bbdb431a7d6b186e8dad1d37e77a4522fe8104b6ce1785ea26bd8c

AARDVARK_VERSION=v2.1.0
AARDVARK_SHA256=c07b42ded1ad43d722143791fb0323f91bad3259d13774120e54321d018b760e

# catatonit's newest release is v0.2.1, dated 2024-12-14 — a year and eight
# months old at the time of pinning. That is the cadence of a few-hundred-KB
# container init, not evidence of abandonment, but it is the slowest-moving
# thing this build carries and it belongs in PLAN-012's supply-chain risks
# rather than in nobody's head.
CATATONIT_VERSION=v0.2.1
CATATONIT_SHA256=2c43bfd6a3466dc6d23355956f6f8dc4dba8c75706ee9eb802eaaaa62d58d7f5
